; Native Megalodon (Mathdata) proofs.  Import with (import! &self megalodon).
;
; Theories, authority, theorems and sessions are opaque values: they print
; as (Sealed megalodon-theory), (Sealed megalodon-authority), (Sealed
; megalodon-theorem) and (Sealed megalodon-session), and no printed text,
; number or data rebuilds one.  Every other value is ordinary data in the
; wire syntax of the Lean contract (NativeSyntaxWire, NativeCursorWire):
;   types       (Tp.var I) (Tp.prop) (Tp.base I) (Tp.arr A B) (Tp.all A)
;   terms       (Tm.db I) (Tm.named "N") (Tm.prim I) (Tm.app F X)
;               (Tm.lam A B) (Tm.imp P Q) (Tm.all A B) (Tm.typeApp M A)
;               (Tm.typeLam M) (Tm.typeAll M)
;   proofs      (Pf.hyp I) (Pf.known "N") (Pf.termApp D M) (Pf.proofApp D E)
;               (Pf.proofLam P D) (Pf.termLam A D) (Pf.typeApp D A)
;               (Pf.typeLam D)
;   contexts    (Megalodon.context DEPTH (types A0 ..) (hypotheses H0 ..)),
;               innermost first
;   rows        (Megalodon.row (Megalodon.judgment CONTEXT P) WITNESS
;                              (parents ADDRESS ..) ORIGIN),
;               stored in a space as (Megalodon.node ADDRESS ROW)
; Judgments: under lazy conversion (the default; see mg:set-conversion) a
; theorem states its judgment in source form, convertible to the reference
; rule's normal-form judgment, which is never built; every rule decides up
; to conversion with the reference verdict.  Its portable evidence ends in
; (conversion lazy) and is rechecked by a lazy session.
; Only the native kernel creates theorems: the functions below are callers
; of checked operations, and a refused rule is an error
; (Error CALL (MegalodonRefused "reason")).  Exhausted budgets, resource
; stops, denied or conflicting publication and unfinished sessions have
; their own error heads; none of them is a refusal.  docs/megalodon.txt
; describes the document checker built on these operations.

